subQuestions.questionText:
The letters A to H in a table represent organic compounds:
A = butane (CH₃CH₂CH₂CH₃, drawn as a full structural formula);
B = a branched brominated compound with the structure H₂C=CH–CBr₂–CH₃ shown as a full structural formula (contains a C=C double bond and two Br atoms);
C = Butanone;
D = C₄H₁₀O;
E = CH₃C(CH₃)₂C≡CCH₃;
F = CH₃COO(CH₂)₂CH₃;
G = C₄H₈O₂;
H = CH₃C(CH₃)₂CH₂CH₃.
Write down the LETTER that represents an alcohol. *(Refer to the table of structures in the original question paper.)*
